Manifests for deploying the Kubernetes NFS CSI driver on OpenShift 4.20
(user-provisioned / disconnected-friendly layout in this repository).

Upstream project: https://github.com/kubernetes-csi/csi-driver-nfs
Upstream release tag: v4.13.2
OpenShift version this bundle is aligned with: 4.20

Core install (apply first, in order):
  1. rbac-csi-nfs.yaml
  2. csi-nfs-driverinfo.yaml
  3. csi-nfs-controller.yaml
  4. csi-nfs-node.yaml

Optional snapshot support (apply only if your cluster does not already ship
equivalent snapshot CRDs/controller; see docs/NFS_OVER_LVM_TWO_NODE_DEPLOYMENT.md):
  5. crd-csi-snapshot.yaml
  6. rbac-snapshot-controller.yaml
  7. csi-snapshot-controller.yaml
  8. snapshotclass.yaml

Not vendored (use Phase D in the doc instead of upstream defaults):
  - storageclass.yaml (example only; conflicts with in-cluster NFS StorageClass)

Upstream path in csi-driver-nfs repo: deploy/v4.13.2/

Upstream license: Apache License 2.0
https://github.com/kubernetes-csi/csi-driver-nfs/blob/master/LICENSE

oc-mirror fragment for these images (merge with your main ImageSetConfiguration):
  ../../imagesetconfigs/nfs-csi-openshift-4_20-additionalImages.yaml

Refresh: replace files from the same upstream deploy/<tag>/ when bumping the
driver or rebasing for a newer OpenShift minor release.
